+## Verdict
+Accept the design as written: name the fix round's 290-of-260 shortfall in the fix template's comment, raise no `timeout-minutes`, and do not shorten the fix session at (e); the shortfall is pre-existing, unchanged by this change, and the intent allows "names" as the answer.
+
+## Why
+- The arithmetic holds against the code: `template/.github/workflows/sdlc-fix.yml:138` sets `timeout-minutes: 260` and its comment counts only 185 + 50 + 10; `plugin/ci/run_phase.py:3180` runs `base_update.update_before_offer` when `gate_phase == "e"`, and `base_update.recheck` runs the three targets at `command_timeout` each (45 minutes worst case, only when the default branch moved). Today 45 + 185 + 50 + 10 = 290; with a 300 s drive 45 + 180 + 55 + 10 = 290. `build_caps_refusal` (run_phase.py:365) still passes: 245 and 250 are under 260, so the build caps keep applying.
+- The intent settles the shape of the answer: "The design raises no `timeout-minutes` it can avoid (the fix template is on the port list) and says which of these it fixes and which it names" (intent.md:88-89), and its open question asks only "what the design does about ... a fix round at (e)" (intent.md:212-215). Spec R4 and the second "Open questions from intent" answer say "named, not fixed"; that is one of the two outcomes the intent permits.
+- Shortening the fix session would reopen decision 32 (the build caps, 180 minutes, for "the build run and every fix round"), which `docs/decisions/index.md` says not to reopen without asking, and `gate.build_max_wall_clock_minutes` is the owner's `sdlc.yaml` guardrail in any case. Raising the job's timeout is refused by the intent's constraint. Coding-standards rule 3 (one change, one concern) also weighs against fixing a shortfall this change did not cause.
+- By REVIEW.md, Important is a finding that would break behavior: the change leaves every figure for the fix round where it is today (290 with or without a drive) and makes the omission visible in the comment, which is better than today's comment that counts it as "with room". Nothing is broken that was not broken before; this is a design note for the owner, not a defect.
+- Safest reading for the build: keep the comment honest (name the 45 of R51 and the 290), and let the owner, who holds the template, raise `timeout-minutes` and `SDLC_JOB_TIMEOUT_MINUTES` together to 305 or more in a reviewed PR if wanted; that is the remedy `build_caps_refusal`'s own message already prescribes.
diff --git a/changes/0004-drive-target-and-proof-items/evidence/panel/b-3-advocate.md b/changes/0004-drive-target-and-proof-items/evidence/panel/b-3-advocate.md
